 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Both simp lemmas take `p : TotalSpace G P` and state their left-hand side as `diffeomorphOfEquivariant G e he hf (ManifoldTotalSpace.homeomorph G P p)`. The neighbouring Principal.lean and Submersion.lean API, e.g. `contMDiff_proj` and `contMDiffOn_trivializationOfSection`, is phrased via `((homeomorph F E).symm x).proj`. That projection is what B1.2's pullback comparisons consume.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/FiberBundle/Equivariant.lean",
   "fix": "Add lemmas for a general point: `(homeomorph G Q).symm (diffeomorphOfEquivariant G e he hf x) = \u27e8((homeomorph G P).symm x).proj, e _ ((homeomorph G P).symm x).2\u27e9` and the matching `symm` statement. Also add a simp-tagged projection lemma, `((homeomorph G Q).symm (diffeomorphOfEquivariant G e he hf x)).proj = ((homeomorph G P).symm x).proj`, plus its inverse version.",
   "issue": "`diffeomorphOfEquivariant_apply` and `diffeomorphOfEquivariant_symm_apply` only match arguments of the literal form `ManifoldTotalSpace.homeomorph G P p` (respectively `\u2026 G Q q`). Neighbouring API, this file's own `hf` and the `toFun` body all work with a general `x : ManifoldTotalSpace G P` read through `(homeomorph G P).symm x`. For such an `x`, no lemma evaluates the map or its inverse, and none states that it lies over the identity of `B`.",
   "line": 156
  }
 ],
